    "final_text": "I fixed ISSUE-214: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`. The full suite passes (`npm test`, 13 of 13).\n\n**Root cause:** in `src/url-builder.js`, the query serializer skipped any \"falsy\" value. `serializeQuery` did it with `if (!value) continue;` (line 126) and `appendQueryValue` did it for array items with `if (!item) continue;` (line 137). The check was only meant to drop missing values, but it also dropped `0`, `false` and `''`. `buildSignedUrl` builds its URL through `buildUrl`, so it had the same bug.\n\n**Fix:** a two-line change. Both checks now skip only `undefined` and `null`, the same check `normalizePath` already uses for path segments. The issue's repro now gives `?dry_run=true&include_archived=false&retry=0`.\n\n**Tests** (6 added in `tests/url-builder.test.js`):\n- Four fail on the old code and pass with the fix: the exact case from the issue, `0`/`false`/`''` inside arrays, an empty string on its own, and a signed URL containing `retry=0`.\n- Two check that `null`/`undefined` are still left out, including that no `?` is added when every value is missing. To confirm these tests actually guard something, I removed the check in a temp copy and both failed.\n- A separate check showed the caller's query object isn't modified.\n\n**Behavior changes:**\n- An empty string (`{ q: '' }`) now produces `q=` instead of being dropped. That follows from treating only `null`/`undefined` as missing, and it's noted in `ISSUE.md`.\n- `NaN` now comes out as `key=NaN` instead of being dropped. I didn't add special handling for it, since passing `NaN` is already a mistake by the caller.\n\n`ISSUE.md` has a new `Resolution` section naming the fixed code path and the regression tests. The project has no linter configured. I didn't commit anything; the changes are uncommitted on `main`.",
